.TH SONICTERM 1 "" "SonicTerm" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sonicterm \- GPU-accelerated terminal emulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sonicterm
[\fIOPTION\fR...]
[(\fB\-e\fR | \fB\-\-command\fR | \fB\-\-\fR) \fIPROGRAM\fR [\fIARG\fR...]]
.br
.B sonicterm \-\-open\-script
.I PATH
.br
.B sonicterm \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sonicterm
opens a terminal window. Without a program it runs the user's shell; with
.BR \-e ,
.B \-\-command
or
.B \-\-
it runs
.I PROGRAM
directly, with no shell, passing every later argument to it unchanged.
Each invocation starts a new process with its own window.
.PP
Options are read only before the first
.BR \-e ,
.B \-\-command
or
.BR \-\- .
Everything after it belongs to the program, including words that look like
SonicTerm options.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-T " TITLE"
Set the window title and the first tab's label. The value is taken verbatim,
even when it starts with a dash.
.TP
.BI \-\-title= TITLE
Same as
.BR \-T .
.TP
.BI \-\-dir= PATH ", \-\-working\-directory=" PATH
Start the first tab in
.IR PATH .
A relative path resolves against the current directory. The directory must exist.
.TP
.B \-\-hold
Keep the first pane open after its process exits, and show how it exited.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-command ", " \-\- " \fIPROGRAM\fR [\fIARG\fR...]"
Run
.I PROGRAM
with its arguments instead of the shell.
.I PROGRAM
is one program name: \fB\-e "cmd args"\fR names a program called
.IR "cmd args" .
A name without a slash is searched on
.BR PATH ;
a relative path resolves against the first tab's directory. A text file runs
only when it starts with
.BR #! .
.TP
.BI \-\-open\-script " PATH"
Open a tab whose shell prompt holds a command that would run
.IR PATH .
The script is not run until the user presses Enter. This option cannot be
combined with any other.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH WORKING DIRECTORY
Without
.BR \-\-dir ,
the first tab starts in the current directory, or in
.B $HOME
when the current directory is unavailable. Later tabs follow the active pane's
reported directory, else
.BR $HOME .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The window closed normally, or
.B \-\-help
was given.
.TP
.B 2
The command line is invalid: an unknown option, a stray argument, a missing or
repeated value, conflicting modes, or a
.B \-\-dir
that is not a directory. Usage is printed to standard error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.sonicterm/sonicterm.toml
User configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR update\-alternatives (1),
.BR xdg\-terminal\-exec (1)
